Falsifies `system_tests::user::map_revocation_window_tests::a_sweep_inside_a_page_frame_map_leaves_no_mapping`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the tree as it stood until 2026-10-04 (UTC): the patch puts `PageFrame::MAP` back to
reading its frame in a critical section of its own, before the seam, and taking the mapping
registry only afterwards to map and record. The sweep held at the seam deletes the capability and
scans a log the mapping is not yet in, and the mapping is recorded after it, alive.

This was the live tree, not an invented break. The revocation-race lane recorded it reasoned at
`syscall::page_frame_map` on 2026-10-04; this test drove it red on aarch64 under both
`PageFrame::REVOKE` and `MemoryRegion::DESTROY` before the fix existed.

Expected to fail: `assert!(!REPORT.mapped.load(..), "a PageFrame::MAP held while a {sweep:?} ran kept its mapping ...")`, on the `Revoke` round.
Replayed red on riscv64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC) against the fixed tree, at
`map_revocation_window_tests.rs:223`, the assertion predicted. Replayed red again on aarch64 on 2026-10-05 (UTC) after main's per-thread table locks (milestone 761 (capability lookup off the global lock)) merged in, at the same line.

**The assertions above the headline stay green under this patch**: the seam was reached, and the
sweep reached the mapper's own table, so the red means the claim rather than the fixture.

Nothing here is architecture-specific: the syscall layer, the sweeps and the seam are portable
code, so one patch serves every leg.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
@@ -24,12 +24,10 @@
     writable: u64,
     ut_slot: u64,
 ) -> Result<i64, Error> {
+    let frame = sched::current_capability(slot).map_err(|_| Error::NoSuchSlot)?;
     #[cfg(feature = "system_tests")]
     crate::delegation_pause::here(); // no lock held
     let mut hold = crate::revoke::hold();
-    let frame = hold
-        .current_capability(slot)
-        .map_err(|_| Error::NoSuchSlot)?;
     let Object::PageFrame(phys, count) = frame.object else {
         return Err(Error::NoSuchSlot);
     };
